window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>He's a warrior of mayhem, a broken alien dragon shifter, and he needs to claim me to be whole again.</p> <p>Taken from everything I knew and dropped in the middle of an alien prison maze, what's a girl to do?</p> <p>Get stuck in of course! My assistance is needed everywhere and I love to help. As for all the huge alien dragon shifter warriors, the Sarkarnii, who rule this part of the maze? I give them a wide berth.</p> <p>All except one.</p> <p>Daeos is a warrior of rebellion. Not trusted by his fellow warriors, watched wherever he goes in case he causes more destruction, forever at risk of exile, this mountain of muscle, scarlet scales and long silver hair has decided I belong to him.</p> <p>I've always been a goody two shoes, I've never so much as got a parking ticket in my entire life, but now I have the warrior from hell pursuing me and it fills me with...Excitement.</p> <p>Daeos is so much more than he appears. Damaged almost to the point of no return, he needs me almost as much as I need him. Only there are forces which want to pull us apart, forces which will stop at nothing to gain control of a warrior such as Daeos.</p> <p>And I'm standing in their way.</p> <p>One of us is going to lose everything and I know it cannot be Daeos, or it will shatter him into pieces. Which means I'm going to have to fight as hard as him, in order for both of us to be free.</p> <p>Daeos is the fourth book in the Fated Mates of the Sarkarnii series from USA TODAY Bestselling Author Hattie Jacks. A broken beast of a warrior who desperately needs to find love and peace, and a sunshine human with a hidden wound only he can heal. Spicy, sweet, funny and delicious, Daeos will capture your heart.</p>"; 
